          "2": {
            "id": "14054028",
            "headline": "SEBI clears IPO plans of Cult.fit, Sohan Lal Commodity Management and 2 others",
            "heading": "SEBI clears IPO plans of Cult.fit, Sohan Lal Commodity Management and 2 others",
            "intro": "While Sohan Lal Commodity Management filed its draft IPO documents through the confidential route in March 2026, Cult.fit, Eswari Global Metal Industries and Indian Gas Exchange (IGX) submitted their draft papers in July 2026.",
            "body": "Sohan Lal Commodity Management, Cult.fit and two other companies have received approval from the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) to proceed with their initial public offering (IPO) plans.\r\n\r\nWhile Sohan Lal Commodity Management filed its draft IPO documents through the confidential route in March 2026, Cult.fit, Eswari Global Metal Industries and Indian Gas Exchange (IGX) submitted their draft papers in July 2026.\r\n\r\nThe capital markets regulator issued its observations on the draft IPO papers of Cult.fit and IGX on October 12, followed by those of Sohan Lal Commodity Management and Eswari Global Metal Industries on October 13.\r\n\r\nSEBI's observations pave the way for companies to launch their IPOs within the prescribed timelines. Companies that follow the regular filing route generally have 12 months from the date of receiving the observations to launch their IPOs, while those opting for the confidential filing route have 18 months.\r\n\r\nFitness and active lifestyle platform Cult.fit, co-founded by Myntra founder Mukesh Bansal, is backed by prominent global investors, including Temasek, Accel and Schroders. The company plans to raise Rs 950 crore through a fresh issue of shares, alongside an offer for sale (OFS), through its proposed IPO.\r\n\r\nExisting investors, including Temasek Holdings-backed MacRitchie Investments, Fitness First Luxembourg, IDG Ventures India Fund, Tata Digital, Chiratae Trust, Schroders Capital, Twenty Nine Capital Partners and Accel India V (Mauritius), are among the proposed selling shareholders. They plan to offload a total of 17.86 crore equity shares through the OFS.\r\n\r\nCult.fit describes itself as India's largest fitness and active lifestyle platform. The company operates 708 fitness centres across 77 cities in India and offers fitness services and active lifestyle products through its app, website and other online and offline channels. As of March 31, 2026, it had more than 9.87 lakh paid members.\r\n\r\nNew Delhi-headquartered Sohan Lal Commodity Management, founded in 2009 by Sandeep Sabharwal, filed its draft IPO papers with SEBI through the confidential route. Consequently, details of its proposed public offering are not available in the public domain.\r\n\r\nFollowing SEBI's observations, the company can proceed with to the next stage of the IPO process by filing an updated draft red herring prospectus (DRHP). It will subsequently file a red herring prospectus (RHP) with the Registrar of Companies before launching the public offering, within the applicable 18-month period from the date of receiving SEBI's observations.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nSohan Lal Commodity Management is a technology-driven post-harvest agri-logistics provider. Its services include commodity management, warehousing, procurement and collateral management of agricultural commodities, along with end-to-end agricultural solutions for Indian farmers and other stakeholders.\r\n\r\nTamil Nadu-based Eswari Global Metal Industries, which recycles and manufactures value-added non-ferrous metal products, plans to raise Rs 500 crore through a fresh issue of equity shares. Existing shareholders, including the promoters, will also sell 1.32 crore equity shares through an OFS.\r\n\r\nIndian Gas Exchange, promoted by power trading platform Indian Energy Exchange (IEX), filed its draft IPO papers in July 2026. The proposed IPO comprises an OFS of 1.67 crore equity shares by promoter IEX, which holds a 47.28 percent stake in the gas exchange.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/sebi-clears-ipo-plans-of-cult-fit-sohan-lal-commodity-management-and-2-others-14054028.html",
            "ai_impact_text_option_s": "Bullet",
